WEBVTT

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:20.620
In order to become stronger at Vanguard 
fights, I have to get some grade 3 cards.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.080
Weak! Too weak!

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.200
Say what?!

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.300
I stand, and draw!

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:41.520
Time for this fight to be over.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.170
What did you say?

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.200
I ride... Asura Kaiser!

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.650
A grade 3?

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.660
Attack, Asura Kaiser!

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:26.830
Finish Hold!

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.280
Now who claimed they'd beat me 
and have the last laugh again?

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:36.000
You lost, so say it.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.630
We can't hear you!

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.390
Don't get all smart just 'cause you won!

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:52.760
What...

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.530
He won, taking only 2 damage.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:02:59.820
Incredible.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.430
Incredible, me?

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.060
No, I'm not incredible.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.250
<i>I</i> am strong!

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:13.210
Cock a nose, 'cause you're listenin' 
to Kamui the Great, number one!

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:16.210
It's cock an ear, not a nose...

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:22.180
This brat's pretty strong when it comes to 
Vanguard fights, but his personality has issues.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.680
You're one to talk.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.650
He doesn't give anyone any respect, whether 
they're grade-schoolers or adults.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:31.420
I'm thinkin' about teaching him about 
respecting seniority and all that...

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.150
As expected, Kamui the Great!

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.270
SS, yo!

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:36.600
Es-es?

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.430
Super-Strong, yo!

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:41.830
He doesn't even know what 
SS means. What a BK.

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:43.340
Dang straight, yo.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.230
BK?

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:46.880
Big knucklehead?

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.920
H-Hey, you brats!

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:51.630
You think he's fought Kai?

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:57.700
Um, would you fight me next?

00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:58.750
What's your name?

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:00.150
Aichi Sendou.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:03.070
Aichi Sendou?

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:04.850
You're weak, ain't ya?

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:05.970
No thanks.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:09.040
I can tell who's strong.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.120
I can't feel a thing from you.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.600
Not gonna get anything from 
beatin' up weak people.

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:17.800
It's true that I've only started 
Vanguard fighting recently,

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:19.610
and I don't have any grade 3s...

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:23.210
Even if you did, you couldn't beat me!

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:25.610
You're a big weenie, Aichi!

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.120
Well, it looks like it's my turn.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.660
The strongest Vanguard Fighter 
in Hitsue Junior High!

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:37.060
I, Katsumi Morikawa, will 
face you one-on-one!

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:39.500
If I win, you start treatin' me with respect!

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:44.960
Sounds like a plan! Then, if 
I win, you gotta do the same!

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.050
Stand up! Vanguard!

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:52.100
Attack, Asura Kaiser!

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.760
I lost...

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.100
Morikawa...

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:00.310
I told you, I'm strong!

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:04.610
He's not just talk. He really is good.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:09.230
29 victories in a row against junior-high 
kids! Impressive, Kamui the Great!

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:12.280
SS, yo! Super-strong, yo!

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:16.720
You're all bluff. You're the 
worst player I've ever beaten.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.810
Today was just a fluke!

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:22.200
The stars were in the worst possible 
alignment, so I couldn't get anything going!

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:26.300
I believe you promised to 
show me some respect, Loser.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.180
Yeah, I did, Mr. Pipsqueak.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.180
Say, what?!

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:34.280
A booster pack, was it?

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:35.770
Right.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.990
I hope you get a grade 3.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:38.690
Yeah.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:42.480
I've bought plenty before, 
but never gotten one.

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:45.690
But this time, I really want to get one!

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.200
I knew this was where you would be!

00:05:58.130 --> 00:05:59.670
Oh, my Goddess!

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:00.830
OMG, yo.

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:03.330
She looked at me!

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:06.340
She's coming over!

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.550
I'm in love!

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:14.500
Miss, if you want to know 
anything about Vanguard,

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:17.100
just ask me, I'm number one! 
I'll teach you anything!

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:22.720
Say "sure" or "I'd love that" or just skip 
straight past bein' friends and be my girlfriend!

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:26.070
You'll say yes, right?

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:31.770
Hey, Aichi!

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:32.570
Emi...

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:35.970
I wonder what kind of relationship they have?

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:37.140
I want to find out!

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:38.460
OK, yo...

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:42.960
Did you forget, Aichi? You promised 
to do homework with me today.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:47.150
I-I'm sorry, Emi. I was planning on coming 
home right after buying a booster pack.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:49.060
I don't care about your 
excuses. Now come with me.

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:50.930
But I haven't bought it yet!

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:52.900
We're leaving, got it?

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:56.280
Aichi? Emi? They call each 
other by first names?

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:58.480
They said they were doing 
homework together, didn't they?

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:01.090
They were linking arms, 
yo... Maybe they're...

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:03.210
Boyfriend and girlfriend?

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:09.650
I'm not even going to bother 
correcting those idiots.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:17.660
Whirlwind! Kamui, the Grade-School Fighter!

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:22.950
Here's your booster pack.

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:24.030
Thank you.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:30.070
I hope there's a grade 3 in here.

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:35.530
Grade 1...

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:37.580
Next...

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:39.810
Grade 2.

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:45.100
Not many cards that seem 
useful for your deck...

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:47.690
How unlucky can you get, Aichi?

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.080
Only one left.

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:59.180
All right! It's the Knight 
of Frivolity, Gancelot!

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:03.480
The grade 3s really have a 
different air to them, you know?

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:06.500
It's a Royal Paladin, like your deck.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:07.990
You got lucky.

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:08.930
Yeah.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:12.590
It's my first grade 3 card!

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:15.800
W-What? A paper bag?

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:18.960
K-Kamui?

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:21.220
Aichi Sendou, we fight!

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.260
Fight?

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:28.480
Didn't you know? When you challenge someone 
to a fight, you have to slap them with a bag!

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:32.970
It's not a bag, you slap them with a glove!

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:36.530
I challenge you to a Vanguard Fight!

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:40.830
But you said you wouldn't fight me yesterday.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:43.700
That was yesterday, and today is today!

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:45.940
I'll win, and get my Goddess!

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:47.780
Goddess?

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:50.680
Do it, Aichi! Get revenge for me!

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:52.170
We're best buds, right?

00:08:56.850 --> 00:09:00.180
I don't really understand, 
but if you'll fight me now...

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:16.190
My hand's full of grade 0s...

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:17.280
What'll I do?

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:20.740
Wait, you don't know about taking a redraw?

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:21.880
A redraw?

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:24.500
You really are a beginner...

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:31.250
Right before beginning, you can return any
unwanted cards to your deck and draw again.

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:33.380
Really?

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:36.300
I told you because I figured you didn't know.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:42.760
You should have at least one grade 1, 2, 
and 3 in your hand. That's basic strategy.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:43.970
I see!

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:47.850
If you have them in your hand, it'll 
be much easier to ride to higher grades.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.480
Thank you for telling me!

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:52.750
Giving your opponent advice? How gallant, yo.

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:55.370
Your Goddess is gonna swoon all over you!

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.290
Then, I'll redraw three cards.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.700
I will also redraw.

00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:10.890
We can no longer redraw.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:12.130
Here we go!

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:12.940
Right!

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:17.010
Stand up! Vanguard!

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:30.710
I can go first, right?

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:33.110
Yeah! I like going second.

00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:37.930
I ride the Little Sage, Marron!

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:46.340
I can't attack on the first 
turn, so I'm done.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:47.370
That's right.

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:53.840
I ride the Screamin' and Dancin' Announcer, Shout!

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:58.280
While riding a Nova Grappler unit on 
top of the same type, Battleraizer,

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:03.190
Battleraizer's ability is activated, and 
it can be moved to a rear-guard circle.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.600
It has that ability?

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:10.060
I call a Queen of Hearts and a Shining Lady!

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:14.660
The reason I like going second... 
is because it lets me attack first!

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:18.610
I support the Queen of Hearts with 
Battleraizer and attack Marron!

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:23.820
With Battleraizer's skill, power 
during this battle is +3000!

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:26.080
I guard with Weapons Dealer Govannon.

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:34.990
I support Shout with Shining 
Lady, and attack Marron!

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:39.170
I defend with the Yggdrasil Maiden, Elaine!

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:41.110
I check for a drive trigger...

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:45.240
No trigger... Thank goodness.

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:54.940
Was defending there really necessary?

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:56.710
My turn's over.

00:11:56.710 --> 00:12:00.040
I'm returning the Battleraizer I 
just used for support to the deck.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:03.240
Your turn!

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:11.540
Stand up, my avatar!

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:15.210
Ride Blaster Blade!

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:20.960
I call Wingal and the Knight 
of Silence, Gallatin!

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:25.980
Listen up. Attack me with all you got.

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:30.360
You can't take damage when you're the one 
attacking. Not attacking would be your loss.

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:34.390
I attack Shout with Gallatin!

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:35.940
I don't defend.

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:38.250
Check for a damage trigger...

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:44.390
I support Blaster Blade with 
Wingal, and attack Shout!

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:48.440
Using Wingal's ability, Blaster 
Blade's power is +4000!

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:52.370
And I check for a drive trigger.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:53.290
No trigger.

00:12:55.050 --> 00:12:56.880
Check for a damage trigger.

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.800
Got a stand trigger.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:06.220
When you get a Lucky Girl trigger, you can 
add +5000 to any unit's power you like.

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:08.400
I apply this power to Shout.

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:12.740
Plus, you can stand one 
of your rear-guard units!

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:14.430
Oh, no!

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:18.530
Huh? But, it's my turn right now, so...

00:13:18.530 --> 00:13:21.350
Yeah! I can't attack.

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:24.230
Phew... That trigger was meaningless.

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:25.860
Dude, those are the basics!

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:29.370
Great timing!

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.080
I ride Hungry Dumpty!

00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:38.070
Also, I move the Queen of Hearts.

00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:40.130
And in its place I call the King of Swords.

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:41.840
Move?

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:44.790
I call Tough Boy and Genocide Jack!

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:50.640
Wow... Genocide Jack is only a grade 
2, but it has an attack power of 11000!

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:56.230
Yup! But it can only attack if 
you pay a cost of 1 per turn.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:59.100
Man, what a pain to use.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.810
You don't get it, do you Loser?

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:02.100
Oh, yeah?

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:06.300
I pay the cost, and rev 
Genocide Jack into high gear!

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:11.140
I support him with Tough Boy, 
and attack Blaster Blade!

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.500
That's a total of 19000!

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.860
I don't want to deplete my hand any more...

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:20.660
If I could have just used 
that Elaine from before...

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:28.710
Check for a damage trigger.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:34.690
I support Hungry Dumpty with Shining 
Lady, and attack Blaster Blade!

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:38.600
Check for a drive trigger.

00:14:40.610 --> 00:14:41.350
Got it!

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:48.360
When Battleraizer activates a trigger, you 
can stand up a unit in a rear-guard circle!

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:49.600
You don't mean...

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:51.710
Exactly! Genocide Jack!

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:55.220
Plus, you can add +5000 to any unit you like!

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:57.500
I also give this power to Genocide Jack!

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.020
16000!

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:05.370
I check for a damage trigger...

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:12.720
And now, I attack Blaster Blade with 
the now-standing Genocide Jack!

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:18.080
Check for a damage trigger...

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.980
No trigger.

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:25.490
I support the King of Swords with the 
Queen of Hearts and attack Blaster Blade!

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:29.990
When the King is supported by 
the Queen, he gets +4000 power!

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:35.160
I see! That's why he moved 
the Queen to the back!

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:38.720
Check for a damage trigger...

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:42.540
4 damage in just this turn...

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.540
Kamui really is strong.

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:48.930
All I can do is attack him 
with everything I have!

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:06.020
That's...

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:07.980
Here it comes.

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:13.450
Give me the power! The proud, 
prideful white wings!

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:15.480
Ride!

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:21.050
Solitary Knight, Gancelot!

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:27.920
I activate Gancelot's counter blast! At 
a cost of 2, I add 5000 to his power!

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:32.910
Plus, critical +1!

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:36.800
And, once more!

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:43.930
Supporting with Marron, I attack 
Hungry Dumpty with Gallatin!

00:16:44.860 --> 00:16:48.160
I have two cards in my hand, and 
only one that I can use as a shield.

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:53.920
If I can defend against this 
attack, I can still take 3 damage.

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:56.780
Gancelot's critical is 3 right now.

00:16:57.390 --> 00:17:01.870
As long as he doesn't draw an Epona during 
the twin drive trigger check, I should be okay.

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:06.700
I can't believe a guy like this 
would have that kind of luck.

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:08.520
Okay!

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:10.250
I defend with Battleraizer!

00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:18.180
I support Gancelot with Wingal, and attack!

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:21.220
Twin Drive! I check for drive triggers...

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:22.270
The first check...

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:23.460
Good.

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:26.560
Draw an Epona! Beat that damn brat!

00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:29.560
The second drive trigger check...

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:35.500
Am I the only one who has the 
super-lucky draw in times like these?

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:40.400
I check for a damage trigger 3 times.

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:41.120
First check.

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:43.870
Clay-doll Mechanic.

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:44.920
No trigger.

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:47.120
Second check, Clay-doll Mechanic.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:50.190
Third check. Invincible.

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:51.460
No trigger.

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:57.220
Only a little more... My turn is over.

00:17:57.770 --> 00:17:59.670
I stand, and draw!

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:01.350
Let's do this!

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:04.890
I ride Asura Kaiser!

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:10.740
Counter Blast activated!

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:12.820
I rev Genocide Jack into high gear!

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:18.620
With support from Tough Boy, I 
attack Gancelot with Genocide Jack!

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:27.370
Check for a damage trigger.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:32.150
Only one left...

00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:36.940
I support the King of Swords with the 
Queen of Hearts, and attack Gancelot!

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:40.700
I guard with Epona!

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:43.760
For the remainder, I intercept with Gallatin!

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:47.850
Intercept?

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:51.310
It's an ability that lets units in 
the front row join in the defense.

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:56.500
I-I knew that! I was just 
checking if <i>you</i> knew that!

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.680
Your attack won't go through now!

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:01.180
Next!

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:05.830
Asura Kaiser, supported by 
Shining Lady, attacks Gancelot!

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:10.990
I guard with Gallatin and Unicorn!

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:16.190
Okay! You can do this!

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:18.170
If I can just get to my turn...

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:22.710
Not yet! Twin Drive! Check 
for a drive trigger.

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:24.010
Check one.

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:25.970
Okay, just one more!

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:34.930
I'm... strong!

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:40.840
Grade 3?  But, yeah! No trigger!

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:44.680
Yes... normally, that is.

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:49.290
But when I have Asura Kaiser 
in my Vanguard circle,

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:52.330
I can stand up a card in a rear-guard circle!

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:53.620
No!

00:19:53.620 --> 00:19:55.940
Secret technique, Hell Stand!

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:58.840
I attack Gancelot with Genocide Jack!

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:09.530
Check for a damage trigger...

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.330
No trigger.

00:20:13.050 --> 00:20:14.380
You win.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:18.460
Kamui's so strong!

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:20.190
The junior-high kids are just weak.

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:22.500
Always excellent, Kamui the Great!

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:25.240
That's 30 wins against junior-high kids, yo!

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:29.530
He's strong, but a different 
kind than Kai or Misaki.

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:33.720
Being able to fight all different 
kinds of people makes Vanguard fun!

00:20:33.720 --> 00:20:38.140
Man, you suck, Aichi. Us 
best buds? In your dreams...

00:20:38.140 --> 00:20:39.090
I'm sorry...

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:44.300
First of all, fighting with a deck that only 
has one grade 3 is weird to begin with.

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:46.740
What? He only had one grade 3?!

00:20:47.150 --> 00:20:50.040
When he finishes that deck 
he'll be dangerous...

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:51.450
But, for now...

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:52.690
Aichi Sendou!

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:56.020
You lost. Now keep your promise.

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.480
Yes, Kamui the Great!

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:59.740
No, I don't care about that!

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:03.730
I-I'll be taking the Goddess, got it?

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:06.440
Um, who do you mean, Goddess?

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:09.090
You know, the girl that 
came to the shop yesterday.

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:13.470
Aichi!

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:20.640
Stay cool, Kamui the Great!

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:21.680
SK, yo!

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:23.960
You're here <i>again</i>, Aichi?

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:25.000
What about your homework?

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:26.200
Not yet.

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:31.080
For Pete's sake... Mom asked me to 
make sure you did your homework.

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:32.410
Just a little while longer...

00:21:32.410 --> 00:21:35.800
He's getting too close to my Goddess!

00:21:35.800 --> 00:21:40.440
I guess it's hard to know which one 
is the older sibling at this rate...

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:44.030
What did you just say?

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:47.770
They're brother and sister. As in, siblings.

00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:49.210
As in...

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:52.660
Siblings?!

00:21:53.150 --> 00:21:54.090
Brother!

00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:55.660
Brother?

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:56.900
Brother Aichi!

00:21:56.900 --> 00:21:57.670
No, wait...

00:21:57.980 --> 00:22:00.230
Please, let me call you Honorable Brother!

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:02.380
W-What!?

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:05.210
Honorable Brother, may I 
give you a shoulder rub?

00:22:05.450 --> 00:22:07.470
Yeah, but I'm not your brother...

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:11.580
Don't say that, my dear Brother Aichi!

00:22:13.950 --> 00:22:15.740
Don't go, Brother!

00:22:15.740 --> 00:22:20.060
Honorable Brother! Elder Brother! Kinsman!

00:23:51.530 --> 00:23:54.780
Brother Aichi, your little 
sister is wonderful!

00:23:54.780 --> 00:23:58.580
Yes! But she's very well organized, 
so she gets angry at me every day.

00:23:58.580 --> 00:24:00.350
She scolds you, right?

00:24:00.350 --> 00:24:01.370
That would be awesome...

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:03.540
Anyway, you're really strong, Kamui.

00:24:04.350 --> 00:24:09.090
I hope I can get more grade 3s soon and 
be able to fight on your level, Kamui.

00:24:09.090 --> 00:24:11.630
Next time: The Mysterious Card Shop!

00:24:11.630 --> 00:24:15.010
Wow, the units are fighting before our eyes!

00:24:15.010 --> 00:24:17.470
Brother, I've pictured it!

00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:19.220
My future together with Miss Emi!
